  "details": "When either of these settings is set to 0 MB, it appears to enforce a \"never download\" behavior rather than treating it as unlimited.\n\nHowever, the current UI does not clearly indicate whether 0 MB means \"unlimited\" or \"do not download,\" and the documentation does not appear to address this distinction either.\n\nIf 0 MB is intentionally designed to force-disable downloading, it would be clearer to represent that state with a label such as \"None\" or \"Disabled\" rather than a numeric value. Conversely, if unlimited behavior is desired, an explicit \"Unlimited\" option should be added as a separate selectable value, distinct from any numeric input.",
